      "english": "And when light came out every day the little boy's mother and his father would quarrel with the shepherd saying: “Why didn't you send our son to us in the evening?",
      "source": "Life of Shenoute - part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.boh_shenoute.leipoldt_ed:1-26",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "**ⲉⲣϣⲁⲛ**ⲟⲩⲁ ⲟⲩⲱϣ ⲉϣⲁϫⲉ ⲉⲣⲟϥ · ϥⲛⲁϫⲟⲟⲥ",
      "english": "If one wants to speak about him, one would say",
